## 10. Key Patterns — Follow These in Every File

### Provider pattern
```dart
// Repository provider
final waterRepositoryProvider = Provider<WaterRepository>((ref) {
  return WaterRepositoryImpl(
    dataSource: WaterDataSource(firestore: FirebaseFirestore.instance),
  );
});

// Use case provider
final addGlassUseCaseProvider = Provider<AddGlass>((ref) {
  return AddGlass(ref.read(waterRepositoryProvider));
});

// State provider
final waterStateProvider = StreamProvider.family<WaterData?, String>((ref, userId) {
  return ref.read(waterRepositoryProvider).watchWaterData(userId);
});
```

### Screen template
```dart
class WaterTrackingScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  const WaterTrackingScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final userId = ref.watch(authUserIdProvider);
    if (userId == null) return const AuthRedirectWidget();

    return Scaffold(
      backgroundColor: Colors.transparent,
      appBar: const WaterTrackingAppBar(),
      body: WaterTrackingBody(userId: userId),
    );
  }
}
```

### Widget template
```dart
// lib/features/water_tracking/presentation/widgets/water_progress_ring.dart

class WaterProgressRing extends StatelessWidget {
  final int consumed;
  final int goal;

  const WaterProgressRing({
    super.key,
    required this.consumed,
    required this.goal,
  });

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    final colors = Theme.of(context).extension<AppColors>()!;
    final progress = goal > 0 ? consumed / goal : 0.0;
    // ... build UI
  }
}
```

### Error and loading states
Each feature should have dedicated error and loading widgets:
```
features/water_tracking/presentation/widgets/
  water_loading_state.dart
  water_error_state.dart
  water_empty_state.dart
```

