## 11. Firebase Firestore Structure (Reference)

```
users/{uid}
  name, email, age, gender, goal, currentWeight, goalWeight, height, ...
  fcmToken: string
  
users/{uid}/daily/{date}
  steps: { steps, goalSteps }
  water: { glassesConsumed, goalGlasses }
  sleep: { hoursSlept, goalHours }
  meal: { calories, caloriesGoal, protein, carbs, fat }

users/{uid}/weight/{date}
  currentWeight, goalWeight, initialWeight, targetDate

users/{uid}/chatbot/{messageId}
  text, isUser, timestamp

users/{uid}/recovery/{date}
  score, sleepContribution, waterContribution, stepsContribution,
  workoutContribution, recommendation

users/{uid}/mood/{date}
  score (1-5), timestamp

challenges/{challengeId}
  title, description, metric, goal, durationDays, startDate, endDate, participantCount

challenges/{challengeId}/participants/{uid}
  joinedAt, currentProgress, completed

chats/{chatId}
  participants, lastMessage, lastMessageAt

chats/{chatId}/messages/{messageId}
  text, senderId, timestamp, status
```

---

## 12. Liquid Glass UI Patterns for Each Screen Type

### Tracking screen pattern
```
GradientBackground
  └── SafeArea
        └── CustomScrollView
              ├── GlassAppBar (sliver)
              ├── HeroAnimation (Lottie — keep existing)
              ├── GlassCard — main metric (large number + circular progress)
              ├── GlassCard — chart section
              ├── GlassCard — tips / info
              └── YeetButton — log entry action
```

### Dashboard pattern
```
GradientBackground
  └── CustomScrollView
        ├── DashboardHeader (greeting + avatar + date)
        ├── RecoveryScoreGauge (large, prominent)
        ├── MoodLogRow (emoji strip)
        ├── DailyProgressGrid (2x2 glass cards: steps/water/sleep/calories)
        └── MealTrackingCard (glass card with macro breakdown)
```

### List screen pattern (Explore, Challenges)
```
GradientBackground
  └── SafeArea
        ├── GlassSearchBar (sticky)
        └── ListView
              └── GlassCard (for each item, with subtle border gradient)
```

---

## 13. Do Not Do

- Do not use `AppTheme.colors[...]` anywhere
- Do not define widgets inside screen files
- Do not hardcode colors with hex values (use `AppColors`)
- Do not hardcode route strings (use constants)
- Do not import Firebase packages in domain layer
- Do not put business logic in widgets (widgets are pure UI)
- Do not use `print()` — use `debugPrint()` or a logging package
- Do not use `Color.withOpacity()` — use `.withValues(alpha:)`
- Do not leave TODO comments in committed code — implement or file an issue

---

*End of brief. When you start each step, state which step you're on and what file you're modifying.*
